WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.560
What if just one
lifestyle change

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.360
could help you
avoid getting cancer,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.200
or diabetes,
or heart disease,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.560
or high blood pressure?

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.920
This one change could cut
your risk of chronic disease

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.680
and add years to your life.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.440
Well, the simple solution to
so many of these problems

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.760
is to eat a healthy diet.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.200
In other words, one centered
around whole plant foods.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.720
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.120
I'm your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.920
Today we look a problem that many
men experience from time to time,

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.480
erectile dysfunction.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.078
And we start by looking
at the nuts.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.240
I’m talking about walnuts,
almonds and hazelnuts.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.000
Here’s the story.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.840
In 2013 — I can't believe it's already
been so long — I posted a video

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.400
based on this study, that found that
three weeks of pistachios resulted

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.000
in a significant improvement
in erectile function in men.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.840
It's always nice to see a whole food
intervention have clinical effects,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.000
and I was curious to revisit the topic
to see what's been published since.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.800
Even if you ignore all the lab
animal studies on, you know,

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.320
how much hazelnuts improve
the function of rat testicles,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.600
you still never know what you'll find
searching the medical literature

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.080
for nuts and sexual function,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.440
like this case of penile
strangulation with a metal hex nut.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.360
I guess nuts can sometimes make
things worse if you can't remove them.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:39.040
They used the Dundee technique, which
involves creating 20 puncture holes

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.600
to relieve the pressure,
but that didn't work.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.520
So a diamond disk cutter
was used to saw through it,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.600
and they slipped a few times.
All's well that ends well.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.920
Well, that got me curious.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.760
Evidently, penile entrapment
is so common,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.000
there's an entire grading system
that emergency room docs can use.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.120
If a drill is not available,
these surgeons advise

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:09.920
a hammer and chisel may be used.
A drill? Oh, a dental drill.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.960
I like how they brag about
the precisely cut edges.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:13.440
Looks pretty jagged to me.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.200
To "preserve the penis
from a fatal outcome"

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.800
(that's a strange way to put it),

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.760
urologists should be aware of all
the available armamentarium,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.600
and if you don't know how
to operate the saw,

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.000
you can always call in
your local blacksmith.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.440
Yet, how are you going to remove a
barbell or steel sledgehammer head?

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.160
A heavy-duty air grinder provided by
the fire department, requiring 6 hours

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.520
of cutting, with the patient protected
from the sparks with fire coats

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.040
whatever it takes.
Hack saw. Cement eater.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.440
Or the silk winding method.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.600
But anyway, back
to the task at hand.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.240
Consumption of at least one serving
of vegetables a day and more than

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.880
two servings of nuts a week
was associated with more than

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.480
a 50% decrease in the probability
of erectile dysfunction

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.360
in a snapshot-in-time
cross-sectional study.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.360
But such observational studies
can't prove cause-and-effect.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.200
It's like finding that men who eat more
healthfully have better swimmers.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.800
Maybe men who eat nuts
are just health nuts,

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.840
and the improvement is due to
some other factor like exercise.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.160
What we need is an interventional
trial, and here we go.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.480
The effect of nut consumption on
semen quality and functionality:

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.800
a randomized controlled trial.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.400
A Standard American Diet, with
or without a handful of walnuts,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.520
and a half handful of each
almonds and hazelnuts.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.000
And the nut group experienced
significant improvements

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.960
in their total sperm count,
vitality, motility, and shape,

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:42.720
perhaps because those
in the nut group

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.480
showed a significant reduction
in SDF: sperm DNA fragmentation.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.440
The nuts appeared to
protect their sperm DNA.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.040
Too bad while they were at it,
they didn't measure the guys'

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.400
erectile and sexual dysfunction.
Oh, but they did!

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.520
The effect of nut consumption on erectile
and sexual function from the same study.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.120
The researchers report that those in
the nut group saw a significant increase

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:12.480
in orgasmic function and sexual desire,
but what about erectile function?

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.360
Any time you see this kind of
selective glass-half-full reporting

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.000
you suspect some kind
of industry funding,

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.520
and indeed that was the case here.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.600
Yes, there was a marginal increase in
orgasmic function and sexual desire

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:31.360
of questionable clinical significance,
but no improvement in erectile function,

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.400
intercourse satisfaction,
or overall satisfaction.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.000
And with so many comparisons,
even the so-called significant findings

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.400
may not even be
statistically significant.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.200
But why did the pistachios
I talked about back in 2013 work,

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.800
while these other nuts didn't?

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.240
Well, if you remember, the
original study was done on men

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.440
in their 40s and 50s who already
had chronic erectile dysfunction,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.120
whereas the average age in
the new study was 24 years old.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.480
So they may have started out
with near-maximum circulation,

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.040
not leaving much
room for the nuts.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.000
In our next story, we look at
how men eating pistachio nuts

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.400
experienced a significant
improvement in blood flow

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.640
through the penis accompanied
by significantly firmer erections.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.400
Here’s the story.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.040
Erectile dysfunction is
considered an important cause

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.520
of decreased quality
of life in men,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.840
in fact, so much so that
one early theory suggested

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.520
that this may
explain the link

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.840
between impotence
and heart attacks.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.960
Depression is a risk factor
for coronary heart disease,

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.880
and the thought was that
men who couldn't get it up

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.160
become so depressed that they
like "die" of a broken heart.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.840
But now we know that erectile
dysfunction and heart disease

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.680
can be two different
manifestations

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.080
of the exact same
root problem,

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.840
DISEASED ARTERIES—

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.480
inflamed, oxidized, cholesterol-clogged
blood vessels.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:55.840
So, no wonder a diet chock
full of anti-inflammatory,

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.320
antioxidant, cholesterol-
lowering plant foods

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.480
would improve sexual functioning

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.640
in both men and women

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.360
as well as reduce risk
of heart disease.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.120
But why go LOW risk when
you can shoot for NO risk?

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.200
A totally
plant-based diet

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.920
can even stop and reverse
our number one killer.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.520
Of all the plant foods
individually examined so far,

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.000
nuts are among those
most tied to longevity.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.520
Just two handfuls a week
may extend a woman's life

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.000
as much as jogging
4 hours a week.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.280
So, if nuts reduce
the risk of heart disease,

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.080
might they also help
with sexual function?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.320
Well, men eating 3 to 4 handfuls
of pistachios a day

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.040
for just 3 weeks experienced
a significant improvement

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.560
in blood flow
through the penis

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.320
accompanied by significantly
firmer erections.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.160
This may not
be surprising.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.640
Remember how antioxidant-rich foods

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.400
have a Viagra-like effect

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.560
of boosting nitric oxide production?

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.720
Well, pistachios are certainly
rich sources of antioxidants.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.200
And remember how the
citruline in watermelons

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.720
helped with erection firmness

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.400
by boosting arginine,

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.960
which is what our body makes
nitric oxide out of?

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.360
Well, pistachios have
a bunch of arginine,

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.240
which may help explain the
improvement in blood flow.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.520
And we know that cholesterol
is an important predictor

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.040
of sexual dysfunction
in both men and women,

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.760
and after just 3 weeks
on all those pistachios

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.680
there were significant
improvements in cholesterol.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.960
And like other studies
that piled on

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.840
hundreds of calories of nuts
a day there was no weight gain.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.800
Conclusion: just 3 weeks
of pistachios

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.840
resulted in a significant
improvement in erectile function

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.520
with additional improvement
in cholesterol

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.360
without any side effects.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.920
Note the 2 important differences

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.360
between diet and drugs.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.720
Just taking drugs like Viagra
to poison this enzyme

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.600
and artificially boost
nitric oxide signaling

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.600
is just covering
up the symptoms

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:54.320
of the underlying problem:
UNHEALTHY ARTERIES.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.960
Whereas eating whole healthy
plant foods like nuts

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:59.600
actually helps attack
the root cause—

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:01.760
cholesterol, oxidation,
and inflammation—

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.320
and only has good
side effects.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:09.520
This enzyme that Viagra-like
drugs muck with

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.000
is primarily found in
2 places in the body:

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.080
the erectile tissue of the penis

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.040
and the retina of the eye.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.760
That's why the FDA
encourages people

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.840
to stop taking
drugs like viagra,

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.680
and call a doctor right away

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.880
if you experience sudden
loss of vision,

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.480
if of course you can
still find your phone.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.720
Though the harms tend to be
self-limited and reversible,

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.800
such as cyanopsia in
which your vision

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.480
suddenly becomes tinted blue.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.520
Why risk side-effects at all,

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.960
when the problem can be reversed,
cured in the first place,

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.680
improving the quality and
quantity of our lives?

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.480
"Improvement of sexual
function in men (and women)"

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.920
"should be added to the growing
list of clinical benefits"

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.280
"brought about by healthy
lifestyles in human beings."

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:04.240
Did you know that dioxins,
endocrine disrupting pollutants,

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:07.360
heavy metals, saturated fat,
and steroids in the meat supply

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.320
may be affecting sperm counts,
semen quality,

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.400
and the ability of
men to conceive?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:19.680
Infertility affects 10--15%
of couples attempting to conceive

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:23.040
and in about half the cases
the problem is found in the man.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.400
A recent Harvard study found that
increasing saturated fat intake just 5%

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:36.160
was associated with a 38%
lower sperm count. But why?

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.800
I've talked about the role of xenoestrogens,
endocrine disrupting industrial pollutants

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:45.280
that build up in animal fat,
particularly fish,

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:51.120
but male fertility is not just
about sperm countâ€”the number of sperm,

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.200
but about how well
the sperms themselves work.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.880
A recent study found that "successful pregnancy
and fertilized egg implantation outcomes"

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:04.480
"are decreased in patients reporting
a more frequent intake of meat."

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.320
"This finding is consistent&nbsp;
with poor semen quality&nbsp;

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:09.920
associated with a higher intake of products"

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.640
that may incorporate these
chemicals and steroids.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.560
"The use of these compounds in the food industry&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.000
results in an increased&nbsp;
total level of xenoestrogens"

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.880
"and sex steroids in processed foods,
such as meat or milk,

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.720
whose intake contributes
significantly to daily exposures".

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.800
"Xenoestrogens are
highly lipophilic substances

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:32.160
that can accumulate in
fat-rich foods, such as meat,"

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.720
"and may be suspected as partially
responsible for the decline in semen quality."

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:42.240
"Conclusion: Couples having trouble
conceiving must be advised"

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:47.440
"about the drastic effect of both the male
and female lifestyle on treatment success."

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.880
This is consistent with previous
findings that frequent intake

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.680
of fat-laden foods like,
meat products and milk

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:58.560
"may negatively affect
semen quality in humans,"

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:02.880
"whereas some fruits or vegetables
may maintain or improve semen quality."

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.360
Vegetable consumption was also
found protective in the new study,

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:11.760
which may be because of the antioxidant
and nutrient content of these plant foods.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:17.120
The adverse effects of meat
could be from other pollutants as well.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.520
Exposure even as an infant
to low levels of dioxin

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.840
can permanently
reduce sperm quality.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:31.840
The general consensus is that human sperm quality
has declined over time in different areas.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:38.400
We're still not sure why,
but dioxins may be playing a causal role.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:46.080
The reason why maternal beef consumption
may alter a man's testicular development

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.760
and adversely affect his future
reproductive capacity

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:53.840
is thought to be due to the anabolic
steroids implanted into the animals,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.120
but as the accompanying
editorial points out,

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.640
the steroids could also be
interacting with other xenobiotic,

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:06.480
meaning industrial chemicals present in meat,
such as pesticides and dioxin-like pollutants,

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:09.840
and even chemicals that may be
present in the plastic wrap.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.360
Heavy metals may
also play a role.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:17.200
Lead and cadmium exposure
as measured in the bloodstream

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.640
was associated with significantly
longer time to conceive.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.840
Where might exposure
be coming from?

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:29.280
Common types of seafood right out of
fish markets and supermarkets were sampled.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.200
The highest cadmium levels were found in tuna;&nbsp;

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:38.080
highest lead levels were&nbsp;
found in scallops and shrimp.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:43.760
The greatest risk from different metals resided in
different fish; some of which got really high.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:48.000
"Thus, the risk information given
to the public (mainly about mercury)

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.000
does not present
a complete picture."

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.320
There are other toxic metals
in fish as well.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:57.360
The largest and oldest fish
had some of the highest levels,

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.400
and we see that with other
animals as well,

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.840
for example, contamination
of beef by cadmium and lead,

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:07.200
clearly dependent on
the age of the animal.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:14.560
The only beverage associated with
infertility in women was soft drinks,

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:19.920
though this may be from an indirect route,
with soda linked to obesity

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:23.360
and then obesity then linked to
reduced fertilization rates,

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:28.080
though there has been a study
on one really direct route,

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:34.880
the effectiveness of Coca Cola as a
spermicidal agent in vaginal douching.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:38.720
Diet coke apparently
had the strongest effect.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:43.760
Harvard researchers publishing
in the New England Journal of Medicine.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.840
What about Coke versus Pepsi?

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.600
Tax-payer money hard at
work for this head to head test.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:56.240
And neither of them really worked -
Coke nor Pepsi,

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:01.120
though they explain their methods for
preparing the sperm-Cola mixtures

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.720
differed from the
Harvard group.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:10.028
Bottomline: soda probably isn't good
for you going into any orifice.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:15.280
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:18.480
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.240
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.560
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:31.680
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.960
please go to the Nutrition Facts Podcast
landing page.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:37.360
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:41.600
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite to each of these topics.

